# Nudge - Richard H. Thaler & Cass R. Sunstein

Richard H. Thaler and Cass R. Sunstein's work introduces libertarian paternalism and choice architecture as frameworks for influencing behavior through environmental design rather than restriction. Small changes in how options are presented can significantly influence decisions, making it part of the Outcomes mental model framework.

## Key Concepts

- **Nudge** — A conceptual tool for navigating complexity via mental shortcuts and deliberate environmental design
- **Libertarian paternalism** — Core principle behind nudging; influencing behavior while preserving freedom of choice
- **Choice architecture** — How options are structured and presented to affect decisions
- **Default effects** — The power of default options and status quo bias
- **Opt-in vs opt-out framing** — How framing changes behavior through structural defaults

